# Supabase

## Clients (do not invent new factories)

| Context | Import |
|---------|--------|
| Browser / client components | `createClient` from `@/lib/supabase/client` |
| Server Components, actions, route handlers | `await createClient()` from `@/lib/supabase/server` |
| Middleware session refresh | `updateSession` from `@/lib/supabase/middleware` |

Use the **anon** key in these clients. Reserve `SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY` for trusted server-only admin work; never expose it to the client.

## Auth / profiles

- Sign up with email, password, and unique company **Driver ID**.
- Pass `driver_id` (and optional `full_name`) in `raw_user_meta_data` so `handle_new_user` can insert `public.profiles`.
- Browser client keeps localStorage sessions for PWA re-launches.
- Middleware must call `auth.getUser()` so cookies refresh for SSR.

## Schema

- Source of truth: `supabase/migrations/*.sql` (start with `001_init.sql`). Apply/verify via Supabase MCP — see `supabase-mcp.mdc`.
- Mirror row shapes in `src/types/database.ts` until generated types exist.
- Core tables: `profiles` (incl. `role`), `loads`, `load_stops`, `load_trailer_history`, `damage_reports` (`asset_type` + `asset_number` + `report_comment`), `damage_notices` (product: viewed), `damage_report_comments` (Feed replies), `safety_inbox_items`.
- View: `damage_reports_with_notice_count` for search UI (`security_invoker`).
- Trailer swaps on `loads.trailer_number` are audited by trigger → `load_trailer_history`.
- Signup always creates `role = driver`; Admin (or service role) promotes safety/admin. `driver_id` unique when not null.

## RLS (current intent)

- Authenticated fleet can read shared load/damage data.
- Damage inserts: drivers only, `reported_by = auth.uid()`.
- Notice (`damage_notices`): any authenticated user can insert/delete own notice.
- Safety inbox: drivers insert for own reports; Safety/Admin select/update.
- Role changes: Admin update policy + trigger `enforce_profile_role_change`.
- Tighten company-scoped policies later — do not weaken insert checks.

## Env names

`NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL` (`https://<ref>.supabase.co`), `NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY` (publishable or legacy anon), `SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY` (server-only). Optional `DATABASE_URL` / `DIRECT_URL` for CLI tooling — see `.env.local.example`.
